# Line endings are a correctness concern in this repo, not a style one.
#
# datasets/ holds generated files that a --check gate regenerates and compares
# against the checked-in copy. With no policy here, the working tree's line
# endings depend on whoever cloned it: git's core.autocrlf defaults to true on
# Windows, which rewrites every LF to CRLF on checkout, and the regenerated
# file then differs from the committed one. That is invisible to anyone whose
# git is set to input or false, and it made the Windows CI leg fail while the
# Linux leg passed (MARVEL-67).
#
# Normalise to LF in the working tree on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except where the tool genuinely requires CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.woff binary
*.eot  binary
*.zip  binary
